{
  "file": "build_pages",
  "spec": "docs/METHODOLOGY.md section 14, amended by sections 15.4 and 18",
  "authorship": "Cases and expected behaviour written by hand by Claude (architect), checked against a separate Claude-only reference implementation, committed by Avi. Codex must never edit this file. The fixture DOC_GBF was produced from synthetic monthly series with the already-verified section 6 and 8 functions, and DOC_GBF_THIN from publish.json's RES_GBF with build_document; both pass check_document. DOC_USA is page.json's. If a case fails and you believe the expected value is wrong, stop and report the case ID and your reasoning.",
  "interface": {
    "module": "scripts/build_pages.py. Load it in tests with importlib.util.spec_from_file_location, as tests/test_runner.py loads scripts/build_data.py.",
    "errors": "PageError is defined in scripts/build_pages.py. WordsError is words.cards.WordsError; RegistryError and PublishError come from pipeline.publish.",
    "write_pages(registry, context, documents, approvals, out_dir)": "Section 14.1 (amended by sections 15.4 and 18). Returns the summary.",
    "main(argv, root, out)": "Section 14.2. Returns the exit code. It has no default arguments."
  },
  "case_fields": {
    "registry / registry_edits": "The registry below, deep-copied, with registry_edits applied with apply_edits.",
    "context / context_edits": "The context below, deep-copied, with context_edits applied with apply_edits.",
    "documents / document_edits": "documents maps an id to a fixture name: that id's document is a deep copy of the named fixture, with document_edits[id] applied with apply_edits if present.",
    "before_files": "Files to create in the output folder before the call: name to text, or {\"folder\": true} for an empty subfolder. The output folder is root/site/data under a new temporary root. For write cases it is created (empty, or with before_files) unless out_dir_missing is true; for cli cases it is created only if before_files is given.",
    "out_dir_missing": "write cases: write_pages is given root/site/data, which does not exist.",
    "page_failure": "{\"call\": n, \"raise\": TypeName, \"message\": text}: replace build_page in the script module (the name write_pages uses) so that its n-th call, counting from 1, raises that type (WordsError or RuntimeError) with that message; every other call goes to the real build_page.",
    "index_read_back_mismatch": "true: replace build_index in the script module so that it returns the real index with its \"assets\" list turned into a tuple. json.dumps writes the tuple as a list, so index.json reads back as a value that is not equal to the index built.",
    "read_back_mismatch": "{\"call\": n}: replace build_page in the script module so that its n-th call returns the real page with its \"claims\" list turned into a tuple. json.dumps writes the tuple as a list, so the file reads back as a value that is not equal to the page built.",
    "approvals / approvals_edits": "Write and cli cases: the named approvals fixture below (\"NONE\" when the case names none), deep-copied, with approvals_edits applied with apply_edits. Write cases pass it to write_pages. Cli cases write it to root/words/headlines.json as json.dumps, unless headlines_missing is true (no file) or headlines_text is given (written exactly).",
    "write_pages_raises": "cli: replace write_pages in the script module with a function that raises RuntimeError(text).",
    "expected_files": "After the call, the output folder holds exactly these names, or null if it must not exist. Each name in expected_pages must hold exactly json.dumps(value, indent=2, sort_keys=True, allow_nan=False, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", where the test builds the value itself from the same edited inputs: <id>.json from build_page(document, facts), with facts the context entry without \"why\", then its \"guided\" set to build_guided(that page, facts) (section 18, words.guided), and its \"headline\" then set to check_approvals(approvals, pages, registry).get(id) (null when absent), the pages in list order; index.json from build_index(registry, pages), with the pages in list order. Every other name holds exactly its before_files text, or is still an empty subfolder.",
    "expected_summary": "write cases: the returned summary, compared exactly.",
    "expected_error / message_equals / message_must_contain / message_must_not_contain": "As in runner.json. message_equals compares the whole message. For cli cases, message_must_contain and message_must_not_contain apply to everything written to out.",
    "cli": "main(argv, root, out) cases: root is a new temporary folder containing pipeline/instruments.json (json.dumps of the registry, or registry_text if given), words/context.json (json.dumps of the context, unless context_missing is true) and data/derived/<id>.json for each entry in documents (json.dumps of the document). out is a StringIO. expected_stdout is the exact list of lines written; expected_exit is the return value; expected_files refers to root/site/data."
  },
